Spec: Todo Service

Purpose:
  Own all business logic for creating, removing, toggling, and filtering TODOs.

Owns:
  todo.js

Must:
  Delegate persistence to StorageService.
  Load todos from storage on construction.
  Persist todos to storage after every mutating operation.
  Support filtering by all, active, and completed states.

Must not:
  Access localStorage directly.
  Perform DOM operations.
  Import component code.

Depends on:
  StorageService
  Todo (model)

Exposes:
  TodoService.add(title)
  TodoService.remove(id)
  TodoService.toggle(id)
  TodoService.getAll()
  TodoService.getFiltered(filter)
  TodoService.clearCompleted()

Handles:
  Empty or whitespace-only title on add — must reject without adding.

Scenario: add valid todo
  Given a non-empty title
  When add is called
  Then a new Todo is appended to the list
  And the list is persisted

Scenario: add empty title
  Given an empty or whitespace title
  When add is called
  Then no todo is added
  And storage is not written

Scenario: toggle todo
  Given an existing todo id
  When toggle is called
  Then the todo's completed state is flipped
  And the list is persisted

Scenario: remove todo
  Given an existing todo id
  When remove is called
  Then the todo is absent from the list
  And the list is persisted

Scenario: clear completed
  When clearCompleted is called
  Then all todos with completed = true are removed
  And the list is persisted

Done when:
  All scenarios have tests.
  No direct localStorage access exists.
  Filtering returns correct subsets for all three filter values.
